      {
        "path": "pkg/core/player/shield/handler.go",
        "facts": "Add overwrites by Type and ShieldTarget. Damage selection uses target and active actor. Expiry uses Expires. Key is not a gameplay branch."
      },
      {
        "path": "pkg/core/sourcehost/shield_lifecycle.go",
        "facts": "Key is copied only to SourceKeyFrame receipt. HP IDs copied to receipt ancestry; all actual receipt fields remain intact."
      },
      {
        "path": "pkg/core/sourcehost/bridge.go:ShieldDamage",
        "facts": "Current HP, damage, shield/incoming elements, bonus and type populate numerical input. HP/Bonus IDs add history components and choose scalar provenance attachment; SourceKeyFrame is not sent to numeric resolver. IDs and all resolver validation remain untouched."
      },
      {
        "path": "packages/sim-core/src/source-host-formula.ts:641-731",
        "facts": "IDs locate and validate prior values and build trace ancestry. Current numerical request is delegated unchanged to resolveSourceHostPlayerShieldRequest. Omission here occurs only in phase-equality projection, never runtime/formula/replay requests."
      },
      {
        "path": "packages/sim-core/src/source-host-shield-formula.ts:23-58",
        "facts": "Formula numerical branch reads request.input HP/damage/bonus/element/output; no receipt ID or shield source key is an arithmetic operand."
      }
    ],
    "limits": "Custom shield types retain their key plus explicit private-state gap, even if they embed Tmpl. Unknown SourceHostDamage descriptors retain an explicit callback gap."
